ene-Placentia is heavily outraised and faces an active investigation headline"], "rationale": "The R+8 district, a sitting Republican incumbent, unanimous expert ratings of Likely R or stronger, and an 85% market price for Hamadeh all point the same direction, and the Democrat's fundraising deficit and the active-investigation headline offer no offsetting evidence. The forecast sits near the fundamentals-implied margin, slightly wider than the baseline given the ratings consensus.", "watch": "Any late-breaking shift in the environment or a major scandal involving Hamadeh could tighten the race, though no polling exists to signal one.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Abraham Hamadeh (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Abraham Hamadeh seeks a second term in this Republican-leaning West Valley district, where the partisan lean favors his party by about eight points. He has out-raised Democratic challenger Bernadette Greene-Placentia by roughly seven to one and holds a modest cash advantage. Every major race rater, from Cook Political Report to Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the seat at Likely R or better, and prediction markets give Hamadeh about an 85% chance of winning.\n\nGreene-Placentia's campaign has drawn wide media attention after she reported being sexually assaulted while repairing campaign signs, but an active investigation into the case has kept the story in the news in ways that may not help her in a red district. With no public general-election polling, the race rests on fundamentals, which all point to a comfortable Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -8.56}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0923, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0824, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1327, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0645, "margin": -10.0}, {"date":